# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets & environment — NEVER commit real keys.
# .env.example templates ARE committed (negated below).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Credentials / certs
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
id_rsa*
*_rsa
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Python
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Node / web
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Go — compiled service binaries (built next to their package)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/gateway/gateway
/alerts/alerts
/journal/journal
/paper/paper
/feedback/feedback
/auth/auth
/bridge/bridge
/bridge/attestel-hermes-bridge
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local Hermes research bridge — WORKER STATE AND CREDENTIALS.
#
# The bridge runs on the owner's own machine. Everything it writes is local: an opaque worker id,
# per-run scratch directories holding the rendered prompts and the raw (unvalidated) model output,
# and whatever the operator points ATTESTEL_WORKER_TOKEN_FILE at. None of it belongs in a public
# repository, and some of it (the token file, a Hermes usage report) would be a real disclosure.
#
# `.env` and `**/.env.*` above already cover env files; these rules cover the rest, plus the
# credential filenames an operator is most likely to reach for. The committed
# `bridge/attestel-hermes-bridge.env.example` is a PLACEHOLDER TEMPLATE and is negated below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/bridge/state/
/bridge/run-*/
**/attestel-hermes-bridge/
worker-id
worker-token
worker-token.txt
*.worker-token
attestel-worker-token*
hermes-usage*.json
!bridge/attestel-hermes-bridge.env.example

# Local Hermes state must never be staged from anywhere in this tree. It is not written here by
# anything in this repository — this is a backstop against a stray copy, an export or a debug dump.
.hermes/
**/.hermes/
auth.json
**/auth.json
hermes-config.yaml
hermes-session*.db
hermes-cron*.db

# Local agent profiles and campaign working material. These are Hermes profile distributions
# (SOUL.md / HERMES.md / config.yaml / distribution.yaml) and the drafts and experiment data that go
# with them — the owner's own operating material, not source for this application. This repository's
# remote is public, so an accidental `git add -A` would publish them; they are excluded here so that
# cannot happen. Remove this rule deliberately if any of it ever becomes something to ship.
/ops/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Runtime state / generated data (mounted volumes; not source)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/
**/data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.pkl
output/
outputs/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tooling / editor / OS junk
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Working backups created during edits (never commit these)
*.bak
*.bak-*
.backups-*/
